hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:2f837e8e189c9885db09005b7de22c29fc874b776af13ec8938a246669e0003d","file":"preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/forcing.tex","line":237,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"1e0b49fe922631183e0ff928e27820d13a133a0fcb3115fe0c385dca0a6eaef7","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/forcing.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:2f837e8e189c9885db09005b7de22c29fc874b776af13ec8938a246669e0003d","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-Partition-Principle-does-not-imply-Choice-September-24-2026/build/sections/forcing.tex#L237"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:symmetric-model}\nThe symmetric forcing relation is definable formula by formula in\n\\(V\\), and it forces every axiom instance of full pure-set \\(\\ZF\\).\nIf \\(V\\) is externally transitive, the evaluated class \\(W\\) is\na transitive model of that theory, with\n\\[\n V\\subseteq W\\subseteq V[F][H],\n \\qquad \\Ord^W=\\Ord^{V[F][H]}.\n\\]\nThe truth lemma holds for this evaluated model.  Over an arbitrary\ncountable choice ground, it holds for the symmetric quotient of internal\nnames described in Section~\\ref{sec:metatheory}."}
